<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dance of Zalongo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1803">1803</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Dance of Zalongo is the name given to the mass suicide of Souliote women on Mount Zalongo in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epirus">Epirus</a> in December 1803, after Ali Pasha of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ioannina">Ioannina</a> had forced Souli to surrender. According to tradition, the women, to avoid capture by his troops, threw their children and then themselves from the cliffs while dancing and singing. The event became a symbol of Greek resistance and is marked by a monument on the site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dance-of-zalongo.jpg" alt="Dance of Zalongo" width="320" height="232" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ary Scheffer (Life time: 1795-1858) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Women_of_Souli_(Scheffer).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
